The bug was caused by a use-after-free regression that occurred when the xHCI driver queued a work item to clear the TT buffer while the USB core was in the process of freeing and reallocating a new device for enumeration. This led to the xHCI driver attempting to access already freed endpoint and device-related pointers, resulting in potential crashes or undefined behavior.

